From a4c8f4e08f2f99450a4d40e945369c31e6f5d5a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:35:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: the all-apps sheet on the right screen keeps its
 background

The sheet background is a child of the apps view, which is already one screen wide and pinned to the chosen screen.
The right screen branch also gave the background a left margin of one screen and a negative right margin, which pushed
it out of its parent: the right drawer showed its icons with no sheet behind them (workspace icons showed through)
while the left one was fine. Use no margins on either screen.

Reported by Ethanol10 on Archfx/duo-de#280 with screenshots.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ic7a839045ac5d304f9e3c76b8a0bd4c7fa1009a6
---
 .../android/launcher3/touch/WorkspaceTouchListener.java    | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/touch/WorkspaceTouchListener.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/touch/WorkspaceTouchListener.java
index e863ad4e75..8158f60b05 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/touch/WorkspaceTouchListener.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/touch/WorkspaceTouchListener.java
@@ -227,10 +227,13 @@ public class WorkspaceTouchListener extends GestureDetector.SimpleOnGestureListe
              // The sheet is exactly one screen wide and never reaches into the hinge
              params.width = screenRect[2] - screenRect[0];
              // Align to right or left based on initialX
+             // The sheet background is a child of the apps view, which is already one screen wide and placed on
+             // the chosen screen: no margins on either side (they pushed the right screen's background out of
+             // its parent, leaving the icons with no sheet behind them).
              if (initialX) {
                  params.gravity = Gravity.END;
-                 backgroundParams.leftMargin = screenRect[0];
-                 backgroundParams.rightMargin = -screenRect[0];
+                 backgroundParams.leftMargin = 0;
+                 backgroundParams.rightMargin = 0;
              } else {
                  params.gravity = Gravity.START;
                  backgroundParams.leftMargin = 0;
-- 
